<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- T-86aa/T-f9ab: application-identifier ONLY, like an ordinary CoreBluetooth app. The earlier set was not what it claimed
     (docs/reviews/T-86aa-review.md finding 4, read from the stock bluetoothd binary):
       com.apple.developer.bluetooth-central-screen-off-scanning  is a real bluetoothd capability flag (screen-off
           scanning, session+0xa9), more than an ordinary central app holds, so it is dropped;
       com.apple.developer.bluetooth-usage, ...-background-modes, ...-advertising-extended-filters  occur in no string
           of bluetoothd nor of the dyld shared cache: nothing reads them. Background modes are Info.plist
           UIBackgroundModes, not an entitlement.
     An ordinary central app needs no Bluetooth entitlement; the access check is a TCC grant (kTCCServiceBluetoothAlways).
     run-plan-overlay.sh refuses a binary whose sealed entitlements differ from this set. -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>application-identifier</key>
	<string>com.pixos.btprobe</string>
</dict>
</plist>
